  "claim": "69 Love Songs are American. The singer who formed a group with Kid Montana is also American.",
  "evidencia": "Page: LD Beghtol. Sentence: LD Beghtol (born 1964, Fort Campbell, Kentucky) is an American musician, art director and writer.\nPage: 69 Love Songs. Sentence: 69 Love Songs is the sixth studio album by American indie pop band The Magnetic Fields, released on September 7, 1999 by Merge Records.\nPage: Flare Acoustic Arts League. Sentence: Flare Acoustic Arts League — a.k.a. Flare (band) — were an experimental pop band formed by guitarist Damian Costilla and singer LD Beghtol in New York in 1996 who made intense, darkly romantic, atmospheric songs deeply influenced by their love of The Smiths, The Magnetic Fields (with whom beghtol sometimes collaborated), Love, various 4AD bands and The Velvet Underground.\nPage: Kid Montana. Sentence: Following this, he was joined by American singer Dudley Kludt (The Magnetic Fields, Flare Acoustic Arts League) for the remainder of the group's lifetime.",
