        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0ad1f049-2b9a-5692-82de-2dffc6b29f1a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: LD Beghtol, Damian Costilla, Dudley Kludt\n- Bands: The Magnetic Fields, Flare Acoustic Arts League, Kid Montana\n- Albums: 69 Love Songs\n- Companies: Merge Records\n- Places: Fort Campbell, Kentucky, New York\n- Topics: American musicians, experimental pop, indie pop\n\nFacts:\n- LD Beghtol was born in 1964 in Fort Campbell, Kentucky.\n- LD Beghtol is an American musician, art director, and writer.\n- Flare Acoustic Arts League, also known as Flare, was formed in New York in 1996 by guitarist Damian Costilla and singer LD Beghtol.\n- Flare Acoustic Arts League was an experimental pop band known for intense, darkly romantic, atmospheric songs.\n- Flare Acoustic Arts League was influenced by The Smiths, The Magnetic Fields, Love, various 4AD bands, and The Velvet Underground.\n- LD Beghtol sometimes collaborated with The Magnetic Fields.\n- The Magnetic Fields is an American indie pop band.\n- The Magnetic Fields released its sixth studio album, 69 Love Songs, on September 7, 1999 through Merge Records.\n- Dudley Kludt was an American singer associated with The Magnetic Fields and Flare Acoustic Arts League.\n- Dudley Kludt later joined Kid Montana for the remainder of that group's lifetime.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
